  "query_preview": "..The last part of the weekend atmospheric river/heavy\nrain event is pushing through early this morning with light to \nmoderate rain as the upper level trof and associated cold front \npushes to the east-southeast. Most of this shower activity will\nbe over by 9 am. The heavy rain this weekend has led to some \nsignificant rises on some of our mainstem rivers, creeks and \nwashes. See hydro section below for additional details. \n\nDry for the rest of the week into the weekend. Weak ridging moves\nthrough on Tuesday, then westerly flow on Wednesday as a system\nmoves through the Great Basin. Weak trofiness remains over the \narea Thursday and Friday with upper level ridging building in \nthis weekend. \n\nHighs today will run 5 to 15 degrees below normal. Highs Tuesday\nthrough this upcoming weekend will mostly run 3 to 8 degrees \nbelow normal.",
